 minister without portfolio, representing the interests of Manitoba's francophone community."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02", "start": 649, "end": 674, "text": "Marcoux was re-elected in"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03", "start": 0, "end": 117, "text": "Yvon Marcoux Yvon Marcoux (born March 26, 1941 in Lévis, Quebec) is a politician and administrator in Quebec, Canada."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03", "start": 118, "end": 264, "text": "He was the Member of the National Assembly of Quebec (MNA) for the riding of Vaudreuil from 1998 to 2014, as a member of the Quebec Liberal Party."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03", "start": 265, "end": 336, "text": "He is also a former Minister of Justice in the Jean Charest government."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03", "start": 337, "end": 498, "text": "Marcoux studied at the Université Laval and obtained a bachelor's degree in arts as well as a licence in law in 1963 and obtained another diploma in law in 1996."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03", "start": 499, "end": 544, "text": "He was admitted to the Bar of Quebec in 1964."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d04", "start": 0, "end": 596, "text": "cronica_vita_di_cola_di_rienzo – cucca – cummins – cuneo – cuoco – cuomo – curiel – curti – curti_pier_ambrogio – cusani – cyrano_de_bergerac – dadone – dall_ongaro – dalmasso – dandrieu – danti – darwin – darwin_erasmus – daudet – dauli – da_ponte – da_porto – da_verona – debay – debenedetti – debussy – deledda – delibes – delius – della_casa – della_chiesa – della_porta – della_seta – della_valle – della_valle_pietro – delpino – del_lungo – del_lungo_carlo – dering – desanctis – descalzo – descartes – descuret – despres – devienne – dewey – de_amicis – de_angelis – de_astis – de_blasio –"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d00:c0", "entity": "Marcoux", "scope": "political party", "claim": "Marcoux belongs to the Liberal-Progressives political party.", "answer": "Liberal-Progressives", "quote": "He was a Liberal by background, and became a member of the Liberal-Progressives following the merger of the two constituent parties.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d01:c0", "entity": "Marcoux", "scope": "political party", "claim": "Marcoux belongs to the Liberal-Progressives political party.", "answer": "Liberal-Progressives", "quote": "He was a Liberal by background , and became a member of the Liberal-Progressives", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d02:c0", "entity": "Marcoux", "scope": "political party", "claim": "Marcoux belongs to the Conservative party.", "answer": "Conservative", "quote": "He was a Conservative by background, and remained loyal to the party even after the merger of the Liberals and Progressives.", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0128-30efe7ae49f5:d03:c0", "entity": "Marcoux", "scope": "political party", "claim": "Marcoux belongs to the Quebec Liberal Party.", "answer": "Quebec Liberal Party", "quote": "He was the Member of the National Assembly of Quebec (MNA) for the riding of Vaudreuil from 1998 to 2014, as a member of the Quebec Liberal Party.", "original_document_number": 4}], "current_answers": ["Liberal-Progressives", "Conservative", "Quebec Liberal Party"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Liberal-Progressives", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Conservative", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "Quebec Liberal Party", "origin": "in